---
import Resumen from "../../layouts/Resumen.astro";
import { MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS_PER_SUBSCRIBER } from "../../lib/subscriber/policy.ts";

/**
 * The link was good and the account is full.
 *
 * **This page is only ever reached by somebody holding a live link out of their own inbox**,
 * which is what makes it safe to say something the signup form may not. The form refuses a
 * capped address silently, behind the identical response, because "this address already holds
 * three searches" is a fact about the address and saying it to whoever typed it is the
 * enumeration oracle. Here the address has just proved it is theirs.
 *
 * A subscriber can reach it despite `refuseSignup()` having checked the cap a moment before
 * the mail went out: up to seven days pass in between, and somebody who signed up four times
 * in a week gets four links. The fourth finds a full account, and that is not a failure — it
 * is the cap doing its job at the only moment it can be enforced for certain.
 *
 * `CONTEXT.md` gives the reason the cap exists at all, and it is worth repeating to the
 * person hitting it: three searches is what keeps "dogs in Caracas" and "cats in Maracay"
 * from being two inboxes.
 */
---

<Resumen title="Ya tienes tres búsquedas" heading="Ya tienes tres búsquedas guardadas">
  <p data-testid="subscription-cap">
    Con un mismo correo se pueden guardar {MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS_PER_SUBSCRIBER} búsquedas, y ya
    las tienes todas. Esta no la pudimos agregar.
  </p>

  <p>
    Tus {MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS_PER_SUBSCRIBER} búsquedas siguen igual y el resumen te llega como
    siempre. Si quieres cambiar una por esta, el enlace para manejarlas viene al final de cada
    resumen que te mandamos.
  </p>

  <p>
    <!--
      The manage page is issue #62 and does not exist yet, so this points at the digest footer
      rather than at a route that would 404. ADR 0010 already makes that footer the guaranteed
      live link for a subscriber who holds nothing else.
    -->
    El tope existe para que el resumen siga siendo un solo correo a la semana en vez de varios.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/resumen">Volver al formulario</a></p>
</Resumen>
